Problem Statement: My Pocket Money Tracker 💰

1. Imagine your parents give you pocket money to spend on snacks, chocolates,
 toys, stationery, or games.

2. You want to keep track of the money you spend and make sure you don't exceed
 your budget.

3. Create a Python program that asks for your name and your total pocket money
 budget.

4. Enter the details of three things you spent money on, including the category
 and amount for each expense.

5. Calculate the total amount you spent.

6. Calculate how much pocket money you have left.

7. Display your name, all three expenses, total spending, and remaining pocket
money.

8. Check whether you stayed within your budget or spent more than your budget.

9. Display the appropriate message: "Within Budget" or "Budget Exceeded".

Your challenge: Build your own Pocket Money Tracker using Python! 🚀